  "measures": [
    {
      "name": "Public Measure FC - Central DeWitt Community School District General Obligation Bonds",
      "jurisdiction": "Central DeWitt Community School District",
      "ballotLanguage": "Shall the Board of Directors of the Central DeWitt Community School District in the County of Clinton, State of Iowa, be authorized to contract indebtedness and issue General Obligation Bonds in an amount not to exceed $33,700,000 to provide funds to build, furnish, and equip an addition to the main campus building, including a secure entrance, high school academic wing, and site improvements; and to remodel, repair, improve, and equip the main campus building to serve all students, including educational and administrative spaces, and HVAC, plumbing, roofing, and accessibility improvements, including parking and site improvements?"
    },
    {
      "name": "Public Measure NC - Kirkwood Community College General Obligation Bonds",
      "jurisdiction": "Kirkwood Community College (Merged Area X)",
      "ballotLanguage": "Shall Kirkwood Community College (Merged Area X) in the Counties of Benton, Black Hawk, Buchanan, Cedar, Clinton, Delaware, Dubuque, Iowa, Jackson, Jefferson, Johnson, Jones, Keokuk, Linn, Louisa, Poweshiek, Tama, and Washington, be authorized to renovate, improve, erect, and equip facilities to modernize learning spaces with an emphasis on health sciences, industrial technologies, agricultural sciences, and business and information technology, contract indebtedness therefor, and issue General Obligation Bonds in an amount not exceeding $88,000,000 for those purposes?"
    },
    {
      "name": "Public Measure LJ - Easton Valley Community School District General Obligation Bonds",
      "jurisdiction": "Easton Valley Community School District",
      "ballotLanguage": "Shall the Board of Directors of the Easton Valley Community School District, in the Counties of Clinton and Jackson, State of Iowa, be authorized to contract indebtedness and issue general obligation bonds in an amount not exceeding $7,500,000 for the purposes of acquiring, furnishing, equipping, constructing, and improving the School District's school buildings to include a new gymnasium and new locker room facilities that include a FEMA-rated storm shelter, performing arts upgrades to the existing gym, ADA updates, and other related building, site and land improvements?"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Read in a real browser from the official Public Notice of General Election (signed by Auditor David Troester) on elections.clintoncounty-ia.gov; 55 precinct sample ballot PDFs are also posted. Supervisors elected at large, vote for two. Township trustee/clerk offices for Brookfield, Deep Creek, DeWitt, Elk River, Liberty, Olive, Orange, Sharon, Spring Rock, Washington, Waterford and Welton Townships, plus Hampshire Township Trustee, have no printed candidates (write-in only); the notice says vote for no more than one for each township office. Elk River Township Clerk is to fill a vacancy (the notice does not list a separate full-term Elk River clerk). Public measures: Central DeWitt CSD (FC), Kirkwood Community College (NC; Sharon Township - Kirkwood ballot style) and Easton Valley CSD (LJ)."
}